**Diagram dictionary.** Read a planar diagram bottom to top. A local dot on strand $a$ is $x_a$, a crossing of strands $a,a+1$ is $	au_a$, the identity is the collection of straight diagrams $e(
u)$, and vertical concatenation of diagrams with matching bottom labels $
u$ and top labels $s_{a_r}\cdots s_{a_1}
u$ is the algebra product: in $ab$ the diagram for $b$ is placed below the diagram for $a$, matching operator composition. Isotopies of the plane that do not change the combinatorial type act as the identity, and the local relations (2.3)-(2.8) of Khovanov–Lauda I (quadratic relation, dot-sliding over a crossing, and the braid relation) in the simply-laced Khovanov–Lauda parameter specialization are relations (4), (6) and (7); for general $Q$ the local diagram relations are defined by the full presentation of [[def-quiver-hecke-klr-algebra-for-a-symmetrizable-cartan-datum]]. In particular the degree of a monomial equals the sum of the individual dot degrees plus the signed sum of the crossing degrees, and a dot contributes $(\alpha_{
